{
  "about": "The texture sets Lapin ships (docs/plan-render.md, S1): physically based maps for a material's Appearance tab, under ui/public/textures/<source>/<id>/. Each set is the source's 1K-JPG download brought down to 512 px on its longer side (JPEG quality 78, macOS sips), its NormalGL as Normal.jpg (OpenGL's green up, as three.js and glTF take it), AmbientOcclusion as AO.jpg, Displacement as Height.jpg. size is the tile's width and height on the model in metres (the source's stated dimensions; where it states none, the image's proportion at 1 m high). Chosen, a set's maps are copied into the project as its images (material.textures), so a project keeps them on any computer and in every export. Hashes written by node scripts/texture-assets.mjs and checked by pnpm check:licenses: every file listed, its hash as shipped, its source's licence in the allowed list, no file shipped that is not listed.",
